From a72134c0b13357822d82b3ab555c6e57550e4811 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 15:55:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3.4: Advanced Search with Filters

Add comprehensive filtering to the advanced search page supporting paper, section,
content type, and year filters. Filter preferences persist to localStorage using
learner-store integration.

New component:
- SearchFilters: Filter UI with checkboxes for paper (1/2), content type
  (lesson/past-paper/model-answer/quiz/reference), section (dynamic from syllabus),
  and year (from available past papers). Includes "Clear all" button and active
  filter indicator.

Enhanced backend:
- Extend SearchEntry interface with optional metadata: paper, section, type, year
- Update search-index.ts to populate these fields for all content types
- Add search filtering logic: matchesFilters() applies all active filters with AND logic
- Add SearchFiltersPreference to learner-store for persistence
- New functions: saveSearchFilters(), getSearchFilters()

Enhanced UI:
- SearchPageClient now displays SearchFilters component in left sidebar (lg:grid-cols-4)
- Results area expanded to lg:col-span-3 for side-by-side layout
- Filter state syncs to localStorage on every change
- Filter preferences restored on page load
- Max-width increased to accommodate filters

Integration:
- search() function now accepts optional SearchFiltersPreference parameter
- Backward compatible: search works without filters (empty filters = no filtering)
- Filter UI integrates seamlessly with existing search flow

Testing:
- All 61 unit tests pass
- All 38 e2e tests pass (including existing search tests)
- Lint clean, no type errors
- Production build verified (780 pages generated)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
